    "critical_passage": "Printed p90/PDFp4 says pi_ij<=pi_i pi_j is sufficient but not necessary for n>2, citing Singh1954. Same page §2.3 distinguishes true variance eq10 from sample unbiased estimate eq11. Scope review does not adopt the unrelated optimization convergence or controlled-design efficiency claims."
  },
  "independent_quantifier_analysis": {
    "true_variance": "SYG all-population double-sum identity equals true design variance and is always nonnegative, irrespective of pair covariance signs.",
    "termwise_nonnegativity": "Under pair positivity, every unordered-pair estimator coefficient -Deltaij/piij is nonnegative iff Deltaij<=0. This guarantees estimator nonnegativity for all samples/populations; termwise guarantee is stronger than total quadratic nonnegativity.",
    "fixed_population": "Existing n2 N4 witness yA=(0,0,1,1) has positive Delta12/Delta34 but estimates0,0,16,16,16,16. Thus positive pair covariance does not force negative estimate for any one particular population. Existing yB yields negative supported estimate -3/2 and true variance1; do not conflate schedules.",
    "universal_populations_n2": "If n2 and all pair inclusion positive, each unordered pair is itself a positive-probability sample and its estimate is -Deltaij/piij times(xi-xj)^2. Nonnegativity for all populations implies Deltaij<=0 by choosing xi!=xj. Thus necessity does hold for this narrower n2/universal-populations quantifier.",
    "universal_populations_n_greater_2_witness": {
      "population_size": 6,
      "sample_size": 3,
      "design": "Partition U into pairs{1,2},{3,4},{5,6}. Support all12 triples consisting of one complete pair plus one element outside that pair, each probability1/12. Each triple has exactly one complete pair, so representation unique and mass sums1.",
      "inclusions": "Each unit appears in4 triples as member of its complete pair and2 triples as singleton, so pi_i=6/12=1/2. Each within-pair joint inclusion is4/12=1/3, giving Delta=1/12>0. Each cross-pair joint inclusion is2/12=1/6, giving Delta=-1/12. All first and second inclusions positive.",
      "complete_quadratic_argument": "For supported triple{a,b,c} with {a,b} the complete pair and x_i=y_i/pi_i, SYG estimate=-(x_a-x_b)^2/4+[(x_a-x_c)^2+(x_b-x_c)^2]/2=(x_c-(x_a+x_b)/2)^2>=0. This holds for every real population vector and every supported sample despite positive within-pair Delta. Hence unrestricted all-populations necessity is false for n>2 in general."
    }
  },
